.DS_Store
.build/
.swiftpm/
# Local checkout choice, kept out of committed policy.
# `Selection.json` is the tracked authority for the default checkout;
# `Selection.local.json` is one developer's delta over it (`add`/`remove`).
# Ignoring it is the whole point: a local expansion must never appear in
# `git status`, and must never be one `git add .` from becoming policy.
# `workspace doctor` and `workspace sync` both name it when it is in effect.
/Selection.local.json
# Materialized org roots — regenerable state written by `workspace sync`.
# The active layout places these beside the checkout (see ARCHITECTURE.md,
# "Materialization layout"); the entries remain transitionally for
# checkouts that materialized inside the clone.
/swift-primitives/
/swift-standards/
/swift-foundations/
/swift-components/
/swift-applications/
.workspace/
# Xcode workspaces are generated or scratch, never authored.
# `institute.xcworkspace` is written by `workspace sync` from Selection.json
# and byte-compared before every write; committing it would let a derived file
# disagree with its source, which is the whole failure mode generation removes.
# `workspace doctor` reports it missing and names the command that writes it.
*.xcworkspace/
# `workspace build --fresh` builds into an isolated derived-data directory
# beside the bundle — that is, here — and removes it afterward. Ignored so a
# build interrupted before cleanup leaves an untracked directory rather than a
# dirty checkout that the next `sync` or `doctor` has to explain.
.workspace-derived-data-*/
# `workspace coherence`'s swiftpm-composed-root build path (Phase 2, issue
# #81) regenerates this directory fresh at the start of every run — never
# byte-compared, always rewritten, so there is no version worth tracking.
/institute-composed-root/
Package.resolved
**/Package.resolved
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
